# --- Instructor-only, never published to students ---
# This repo is PUBLIC and read by enrolled students. CLAUDE.md is an instructor
# process file (repo conventions, publish workflow, what must never be shipped).
# It stays local; the sibling student repo elhamod/IS834_Fall_2026 carries none
# either. The authoritative copy of this guidance lives in IS883_instructor.
CLAUDE.md

# --- Course repo .gitignore template ---
# Copy this, then add repo-specific exclusions at the top WITH a comment saying
# what the directory is, how big it is, and where the surviving copy lives.
# An uncommented exclusion of a large folder is indistinguishable from a mistake.
#
# Example of a repo-specific entry:
#
#   # Pristine read-only Dropbox source mirror (172 MB, incl. 103 MB of .mp4).
#   # Lives in Dropbox; copy material out of it, never edit in place.
#   _source_dropbox/

# --- Cloud-sync artifacts (OneDrive / Dropbox) ---
# fuse_hidden files are left behind when a synced file is deleted while open.
*fuse_hidden*
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
.dropbox
.dropbox.attr

# --- Sync conflict copies ---
# These are duplicates the sync client creates when the same file is edited in
# two places. Ignoring them keeps them out of commits, but they still need to be
# resolved by hand -- one of them holds work that the other does not.
*conflicted copy*
*Conflicted Copy*
*-DESKTOP-*
*-LAPTOP-*

# --- Office lock files ---
# Created while a document is open; vanish on close. Never content.
~$*
*.tmp
*.~vsd*

# --- Python / Jupyter ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.virtual_documents/
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/

# --- Notebook and analysis scratch ---
.cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Editor ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# --- Common heavy media ---
# Uncomment only if the survey shows video dominating the repo AND another copy
# exists. Git stores these badly and they dominate clone time.
# *.mp4
# *.mov
# *.avi
